<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Capdepera</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1231</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Capdepera of 1231 made Muslim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menorca">Menorca</a> a tributary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a>. Agreed at Capdepera on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a> after the Aragonese conquest of that island, it let Menorca's Muslims keep their own rulers, law and religion in return for recognising James as overlord and paying an annual tribute. The arrangement lasted until Alfonso III conquered the island in 1287.</p></div>
